1
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:45,230
Some missions are not a choice.

2
00:11:18,461 --> 00:11:24,461
Mission: Impossible - Fallout is a action, adventure
film directed by Christopher McQuarrie.

3
00:16:57,692 --> 00:17:03,692
When an IMF mission ends badly, the world is faced with dire consequences.

4
00:22:36,923 --> 00:22:42,923
As Ethan Hunt takes it upon himself to fulfill his original briefing,
the CIA begin to question his loyalty and his motives.

5
00:28:16,153 --> 00:28:22,153
The IMF team find themselves in a race against time, hunted by
assassins while trying to prevent a global catastrophe.

6
00:33:55,384 --> 00:34:01,384
Ethan Hunt, played by Tom Cruise.

7
00:39:34,615 --> 00:39:40,615
August Walker, played by Henry Cavill.

8
00:45:13,846 --> 00:45:19,846
Luther Stickell, played by Ving Rhames.

9
00:50:53,076 --> 00:50:59,076
Benji Dunn, played by Simon Pegg.

10
00:56:32,307 --> 00:56:38,307
Ilsa Faust, played by Rebecca Ferguson.

11
01:02:11,538 --> 01:02:17,538
Solomon Lane, played by Sean Harris.

12
01:07:50,769 --> 01:07:56,769
Mission: Impossible – Fallout is a 2018 American action spy film
written and directed by Christopher McQuarrie.

13
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:36,000
It is the sequel to Mission: Impossible – Rogue Nation (2015) and the
sixth installment in the Mission: Impossible film series.

14
01:19:09,230 --> 01:19:15,230
The ensemble cast includes Tom Cruise, Henry Cavill, Ving Rhames, Simon Pegg, Rebecca Ferguson,
Sean Harris, Angela Bassett, Vanessa Kirby, Michelle Monaghan, and Alec Baldwin.

15
01:24:48,461 --> 01:24:54,461
Set two years after the events of Rogue Nation, Fallout follows Impossible Missions Force agent Ethan Hunt (Cruise) and his team in
their efforts to prevent a nuclear attack by terrorist Solomon Lane (Harris) and the mysterious extremist John Lark.

16
01:30:27,692 --> 01:30:33,692
Work on a sequel to Rogue Nation commenced before its 2015 release.

17
01:36:06,923 --> 01:36:12,923
The series' first returning director, McQuarrie intended for Fallout to better explore Ethan's character and emotions, believing previous entries
had left him primarily a cipher for audiences, and to test the limits of Ethan's abilities, morality, and personal relationships.

18
01:41:46,153 --> 01:41:52,153
The script was brief, only 33 pages, serving as an outline driven primarily by the interesting filming
locations and allowing for improvisation and significant changes to scenes throughout filming.

19
01:47:25,384 --> 01:47:31,384
Principal photography began in April 2017, on a $178–180 million budget, in Paris, continuing
on to London, New Zealand, Norway, and the United Arab Emirates by early 2018.

20
01:53:04,615 --> 01:53:10,615
Filming was delayed for several months after Cruise broke his ankle during a stunt, significantly inflating the budget while the
production waited for his return but also providing McQuarrie the opportunity to further develop unfinished scenes in the script.

21
01:58:43,846 --> 01:58:49,846
Mission: Impossible – Fallout premiered in Paris on July 12, 2018, and
was theatrically released in the United States on July 27.

22
02:04:23,076 --> 02:04:29,076
The film garnered universal acclaim, particularly for its
standout setpieces, and received several awards.

23
02:10:02,307 --> 02:10:08,307
It also broke box office records for the series and grossed $791.1 million worldwide, making it the
highest-grossing film in the Mission: Impossible series and the eighth-highest-grossing film of 2018.

24
02:15:41,538 --> 02:15:47,538
Fallout was followed by two sequels: Mission: Impossible – Dead Reckoning Part
One (2023) and Mission: Impossible – The Final Reckoning (2025).

25
02:21:20,769 --> 02:21:26,769
The film explores themes of mask, race against time, london,
england, central intelligence agency (cia), helicopter.
